{"kind":"assert","text":"RC-1 ruling on finding 3f2060f4. floor-ahead and floor-keep stay\n`never`. The table stays at never 6, protocol 5, head 25.\n\nThe property of class `never` is the one of acf85bfa: the bytes\nnever take effect at a later head. The reason at the later head\ncan differ. State it for each of the six in the note:\n- archived, floor-back, scope-refused: the same reason.\n- floor-ahead, floor-keep: the same reason, or floor-back when a\n  later floor reaches the input's floor.\n- late: `repeat` of the refused decision (b550f670, ruling 2).\n\nTests: for floor-ahead and floor-keep, add the path where a\nlater floor reaches or passes the input's floor, and assert\nfloor-back there. Keep the path that you have.\n\nKernel review, docs/kernel.md section 7. `REFUSAL_CLASSES` is an\nexport of the kernel part of `packages/bytes`. I permit it by\nthis act. Reason: a class states a property of the judge, and\nruntime, replay and each client must read the same property. A\ntable outside the kernel is a copy that drifts. dap-foldkit kept\nsuch a copy and had three reasons wrong. The export adds no\nform of section 7.1 and closes no K item. Cite this act in the\nhead's note.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}